scripts/test-lint-literal-counts.md:3:Black-box regression harness for `scripts/lint-literal-counts.py`, invoked as `python3 scripts/lint-literal-counts.py --root "$TMPROOT"` against a `mktemp -d` fixture root with `trap 'rm -rf "$TMPROOT"' EXIT` cleanup. Cases a-s cover: clean prose; single `5 reviewers` violation with message text; fenced-code exemption; same-line allow pragma with reason; empty allow reason rejected; every plural noun in the lint regex; mid-line count exemption; multi-file aggregation; BOM/CRLF normalization; non-UTF-8 internal error; exit-code 2 priority when errors and violations coexist; off-by-one fence close behavior; empty root; lowercase-only `allow`; nested 4-tick/3-tick fence length awareness; git worktree enumeration plus `.gitignore`/`.agents/` exclusion, paired with non-git fallback exclusion and a non-excluded control file; symlink non-following; positional-argument rejection; and untracked-non-ignored markdown coverage (case `s`) — the regression guard for `git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard` so a fresh untracked `.md` cannot bypass the lint under `pass_filenames: false`. The harness uses `assert_case`, `write_md`, `reset_tree`, and `run_lint` helpers, prints `Summary: $PASS passed, $FAIL failed`, exits 0 when all assertions pass, and exits 1 on any assertion failure. It exercises every primary code path: length-aware fence state, BOM/CRLF read posture, allow-pragma parser, exit-code precedence, git-worktree-aware file enumeration, gitignored-dir exclusion, symlink non-following, and argparse's `--root`-only CLI. Wiring expectations are Makefile target `test-lint-literal-counts`, one `test-harnesses-N` shard entry (currently shard 2), and an `agent-lint.toml` exclude for the `.sh` only, mirroring the `test-lint-skill-invocations.sh` precedent.
scripts/test-implement-anti-polling-rule.md:3:Regression harness pinning the AGENTS.md anti-polling-loop rule and its mirror inside `skills/implement/SKILL.md` Step 5.
scripts/test-implement-anti-polling-rule.md:10:- `skills/implement/SKILL.md` — Step 5 now delegates review rounds to the foreground `run-step5-review.sh` launcher, which invokes `review-and-fix.sh`. The harness guards that contract and checks the Step 5 block does not reintroduce `run_in_background: true`.
scripts/test-implement-anti-polling-rule.md:12:Without the Step 5 foreground-call guard, future quick-mode review work could re-introduce the same anti-pattern under time pressure (the failure mode that motivated #1011 in the first place: a 30-minute stale poller waiting on a Codex run that had already failed).
scripts/test-implement-anti-polling-rule.md:18:- The Step 5 block does not contain `run_in_background: true`.
scripts/test-implement-anti-polling-rule.md:35:If you legitimately need to reintroduce background reviewer launches in Step 5, update this harness and document the non-polling wait point in the same PR. The rule's intent must be preserved: no parent-side polling loop waits on a background review job.
skills/fix-issue/scripts/find-lock-issue.md:17:   **Main sync (Step B, only when Step A reports `CLEAN=true`)** — `scripts/check-main-sync.sh` (without fetching) detects committed-but-unpushed commits on local `main` ahead of `origin/main`. When every ahead commit is a `chore(larch-logs): flush *` commit touching only `larch-logs/`, the script may run **`git reset --hard origin/main`**, rewinding local `main` to the cached remote tip (destructive for local-only SHAs on `main`). On success it emits `SYNC_STATUS=reset` from `check-main-sync.sh`; `find-lock-issue.sh` re-emits `MAIN_SYNC_HARD_RESET=true` and `SYNC_STATUS=reset` on its stdout before lock acquisition so transcripts record the branch move. When non-log commits are present, `check-main-sync.sh` exits 1 (`SYNC_STATUS=blocked`) and find-lock maps that to exit 2 with `ELIGIBLE=false` and an `ERROR=` about reconciling local `main` — same exit shape as a dirty-tree abort, with no GitHub mutation. The check is a no-op when the current branch is not `main` (`SYNC_STATUS=not-main`). When `origin/main` **exists** in the local repo, **`SYNC_STATUS=probe-error` (exit 2) blocks lock acquisition** — operators should run `git fetch origin main` and retry. When `origin/main` is **absent** (no resolvable remote ref / fresh checkout), probe-error remains **fail-open** so missing-remote harnesses are not hard-blocked. `preflight.sh` still intentionally fail-opens probe errors for historical setup posture. See `scripts/check-main-sync.md` for the full contract and the relationship to `local-cleanup.sh` Step 3.
