scripts/round-trip-detect.md:9:Inputs are concatenated with newlines. `--text-file PATH` is the required transport for issue bodies, PR bodies, and feature descriptions because those can be large or sensitive; callers should write temp files under their run tmpdir and clean them with their existing traps. `--text-string STR` is restricted to short trusted strings such as issue titles. `--stdin` is available for tests or callers with a pipe-friendly text source. The detector performs case-insensitive body matching with POSIX explicit boundaries, not `\b`, so GNU/BSD grep behavior remains aligned.
